From: siraisisatoru <37771374+siraisisatoru@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:57:35 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] umac_relay: send a root's own unresolved frames on the AP
 VIF

umac_relay_update_tx_metadata() picks the VIF for every frame the host
stack hands to mmwlan_tx_pkt() while relay mode is enabled. A frame
goes to the AP VIF only if its DA is an associated station or is in the
relay table; everything else, including every group addressed frame
(broadcast ARP requests, DHCP, mDNS, IPv6 ND), is tagged for the STA
VIF so a repeater sends it upstream.

A relay root (depth 0, started with root_ap_args) has no STA interface.
mmwlan_tx_pkt() then finds no STA VIF ID and drops the frame with
MMWLAN_VIF_ERROR ("No matching VIF"), so the root cannot send a single
broadcast. In particular it cannot ARP for any station, so IP traffic
started by the root never works and stations only reach it while their
own ARP entry for the root keeps it learned.

On the root, send these frames on the AP VIF instead. Group addressed
frames then use the BSS common STA record, as in plain AP mode. A
unicast DA that is neither associated nor in the relay table is now
dropped by the AP datapath ("No STA record", MMWLAN_NOT_FOUND) instead
of failing VIF lookup; it was undeliverable either way.

Repeaters are unchanged. A repeater's own group addressed frames still
go only upstream. In the morselib RX path they still reach its own BSS:
the parent AP retransmits them to its BSS (umac_relay_process_data_frame()
forwards group addressed frames received on an AP VIF), and the repeater
forwards that copy, received on its STA VIF, down its AP VIF while
dropping it locally because the SA is its own. Also sending them
directly on the repeater AP would give its own stations every frame
twice.
---
 framework/morselib/src/umac/relay/umac_relay.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/framework/morselib/src/umac/relay/umac_relay.c b/framework/morselib/src/umac/relay/umac_relay.c
index 37e9212c..5e1604d4 100644
--- a/framework/morselib/src/umac/relay/umac_relay.c
+++ b/framework/morselib/src/umac/relay/umac_relay.c
@@ -942,6 +942,14 @@ void umac_relay_update_tx_metadata(struct umac_data *umacd,
         goto done;
     }
 
+    /* The root has no upstream STA interface, so everything else (in particular group
+     * addressed frames) goes out on its AP. */
+    if (is_root(data))
+    {
+        metadata->vif = MMWLAN_VIF_AP;
+        goto done;
+    }
+
     if (metadata->vif != MMWLAN_VIF_STA)
     {
         MMLOG_VRB("Rewriting VIF to TX packet via STA VIF\n");
